          "title": "Generosity",
          "text": "Generosity is one of the noblest human virtues. It means being sympathetic towards someone in order to be helpful, being kind and encouraging, and sharing one's money, time, and energy with others to make their lives better without expecting anything in return. In Islam, generosity holds a supreme position, exemplified by the holy Prophet Muhammad (SAW) and his companions. Hazrat Usman (RA) demonstrated supreme generosity by purchasing the well of Bair-e-Roma for public use and donating a thousand camel-loads of food during a severe famine in Medina. True generosity does not depend on wealth alone; sharing a comforting word, smiling at someone, or lending a helping hand to an underprivileged person is equally generous. When individuals practice generosity, poverty is reduced, social harmony flourishes, and humanity becomes united in compassion and love."
