          "independentClause": "An independent clause contains a subject and a predicate and expresses a complete thought. It can stand alone as a sentence (e.g., 'I like spaghetti.').",
          "dependentClause": "A dependent clause contains a subject and a verb but does not express a complete thought. It cannot stand alone and depends on an independent clause (e.g., 'Although I like spaghetti...').",
          "simpleSentence": "A simple sentence consists of only one independent clause with a single subject and predicate.",
          "compoundSentence": "A compound sentence contains at least two independent clauses joined by a coordinating conjunction (FANBOYS: for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so) or a semicolon.",
          "complexSentence": "A complex sentence contains one independent clause and at least one dependent (subordinate) clause connected by a subordinating conjunction (e.g., because, although, since, when, if)."
