      "summary": "This lesson from the KPK Class 10 English textbook highlights the sublime traits of simplicity and humility ingrained in the personality of Hazrat Muhammad (PBUH). He treated the affluent and impoverished alike, never wore distinguishing attire, and disliked when companions stood up in his honor. In his diet and domestic life, he was extraordinarily modest: he never tasted bread made of fine flour and slept on a leather mattress stuffed with coarse date-palm fibers. When he passed away, he left no money, but only a white mule, his weapons, and land donated to charity. Despite governing Arabia, he milked goats, mended clothes and shoes, helped dig trenches, and greeted everyone first. During journeys, he collected firewood himself to avoid privileged treatment. The lesson urges us to embrace the Sunnah of simplicity and humility to eradicate pride, ostentation, and extravagance.",
