      "summary": "In 'The Champions', adapted from Piri Thomas's celebrated short story, two lifelong teenage friends from Lyari, Karachi—Ahmad Ali, a muscular Sheedi slugger, and Gul Sher Khan, a tall, tactical boxer from Khyber Pakhtunkhwa—share an ambition to become world lightweight boxing champions. When both qualify for the national finals where only one can advance to represent Pakistan globally, a painful emotional barrier arises between them. Fearing their bond might suffer, they frankly promise to fight with complete honesty inside the ring. On fight night, before an ecstatic crowd, the two friends unleash three savage, punishing rounds of relentless combinations, refusing to concede an inch despite battered eyes and bleeding noses. However, when the final bell rings and trainers separate them, the two brothers immediately rush into an affectionate embrace. Before the announcer can declare the winner on points, Ali and Gul leave the ring arm-in-arm, proving that their brotherhood is the ultimate victory.",
