          "text": "Once there lived at the foot of a mountain a poor farmer and his aged, widowed mother. They owned a bit of land that supplied them with food. They both led a humble and peaceful life. Shinano, the province where they lived, was governed by a despotic leader who, though a skilled warrior, had a great and cowardly terror of anything suggestive of failing health and strength. This caused him to send out a cruel proclamation: the entire province was given strict orders to immediately put to death all the aged people. The days were barbarous, and the custom of abandoning aged people in mountains was not uncommon. The poor farmer loved his mother with tender reverence, and the cruel decree filled his heart with profound grief.",
