          "num": "7.3",
          "heading": "The Mother's Sacrificial Trail of Twigs",
          "text": "The eyes of the old mother still had light in them, and they noted the reckless hastening of her son from one unfamiliar path to another. Her loving heart grew anxious because her son did not know the mountain's paths and his return alone in the dark might be fraught with perils. She stretched forth her hand to snap twigs from bushes as they passed by. She quietly dropped a handful of twigs every few steps as they climbed up. Thus the narrow trail behind them was dotted at frequent intervals with tiny piles of broken twigs.\n\nAt last the summit was reached. Weary and heart-sick, the youth gently released his burden and prepared a place of comfort as his last duty to the one who had nurtured him. He gathered fallen pine needles to make a soft cushion, spread his coat over it, and wrapped his mother tenderly. With tearful eyes and an aching heart, he bowed low to say farewell. But the mother's gentle voice spoke words of self-effacing guidance: 'My son, your path downward is dark and perilous. Look carefully and follow the path dotted with twigs; they will guide you safely back to our home.'",
