          "num": "7.5",
          "heading": "The Governor's Challenge: A Rope of Ashes",
          "text": "Time passed, and the despotic governor again sent forth an impossible mandate to intimidate his subjects: he demanded that the people of Shinano present him with a rope of ashes. The entire province was plunged into despair. Who could weave a rope out of ashes? In deep sorrow, the farmer confided the tyrant's impossible order to his hidden mother.\n\n'Wait, my son,' she replied gently. 'I will think.' The next day, she instructed him: 'Make a rope of tightly twisted straw, stretch it straight upon a row of flat stones, and burn it on a calm, windless night.' The son followed her advice precisely. When the straw burned down, there lay upon the flat stones a perfect, intact rope of white ashes, holding its shape without crumbling.\n\nThe farmer presented the rope of ashes to the governor. The tyrant marveled at the feat and demanded to know who had conceived such extraordinary wisdom. The youth bowed low and truthfully confessed the whole story—how he had hidden his aged mother and how her lifelong wisdom had solved the riddle.",
