      "summary": "In Walter Malone's renowned inspirational lyric 'Opportunity', the speaker personifies Opportunity to forcefully contradict the gloomy, fatalistic belief that it visits human beings only once in a lifetime. On the contrary, Opportunity proclaims that it stands faithfully outside everyone's door every morning, commanding them to rise, struggle, and conquer. The poem urges individuals never to despair over vanished golden moments or lost opportunities of youth, because each night the records of past failures are completely dissolved, and at sunrise every soul experiences a fresh rebirth. Even if one feels devastated by past sins, moral retribution, or public disgrace, the future remains as immaculate and unwritten as pristine white snow. Reminding mourners and sinners that redemption is always attainable, Opportunity offers a sturdy helping arm to anyone determined to declare 'I can!', guaranteeing that no fallen outcast is ever beyond restoration to human dignity and greatness.",
